      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough was named after Rev. Charles Pitman, a Methodist minister who played a significant role in its early development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitman%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1904, residents of the Pitman Grove voted to incorporate as an autonomous borough, marking a significant shift in its governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
